  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>James Coupar, tailor, is in the directories from 1857 to 1871. He is at No. 3 <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref> in 1857 and 1858, and No. 4 in 1859. From 1860 to 1871 he is at No. 3 <ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Street">Victoria Street</ref>.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>In 1858 Dodd &amp; Graham's <ref target="civic?id=Carlton%20Stables%20%28Bouverie%20Street%29">Carlton Livery Stables</ref> are next to him in Bouverie Street. In Victoria Street, Thomas Stiven, saddler and harness maker, is at No. 1 from 1860 to 1863, and Stephen Dark, bootmaker, at No. 5 from 1861 to 1870. The Noah's Ark boarding house is at No. 5 in 1860, and the <ref target="civic?id=Exmouth%20Arms%20hotel">Exmouth Arms</ref> at No. 1 from 1868 to 1871.</p>
      </div>
